1
00:00:01,160 --> 00:00:02,960
Last time, we met a frog.

2
00:00:03,190 --> 00:00:05,470
It is an amphibian, with moist skin.

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,920
Its outer covering is an observable characteristic.

4
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:10,790
Two more animals to spot!

5
00:00:12,329 --> 00:00:13,679
Today you'll learn…

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,260
How to spot a bird.

7
00:00:15,312 --> 00:00:16,992
What makes a fish a fish.

8
00:00:17,044 --> 00:00:18,854
The fish that hops on land.

9
00:00:19,978 --> 00:00:21,158
Lock in first.

10
00:00:21,388 --> 00:00:23,688
A little frog is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:23,898 --> 00:00:25,078
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:26,377
Look up!

13
00:00:26,637 --> 00:00:27,617
A kingfisher.

14
00:00:27,897 --> 00:00:28,907
It has a beak.

15
00:00:29,207 --> 00:00:30,217
It has wings.

16
00:00:30,487 --> 00:00:31,907
And its outer covering?

17
00:00:33,117 --> 00:00:33,987
Round one.

18
00:00:34,237 --> 00:00:35,717
A penguin has feathers.

19
00:00:35,937 --> 00:00:37,067
It lays eggs.

20
00:00:37,267 --> 00:00:38,527
But it cannot fly!

21
00:00:38,757 --> 00:00:40,107
Is a penguin a bird?

22
00:00:40,377 --> 00:00:41,437
One, yes.

23
00:00:41,657 --> 00:00:42,467
Two, no.

24
00:00:42,697 --> 00:00:44,107
Show me with your fingers.

25
00:00:49,575 --> 00:00:50,525
Locked in!

26
00:00:50,655 --> 00:00:51,535
Two.

27
00:00:51,655 --> 00:00:52,815
Birds fly.

28
00:00:53,065 --> 00:00:54,805
A penguin cannot fly.

29
00:00:54,851 --> 00:00:55,451
One!

30
00:00:55,201 --> 00:00:57,321
It has a beak and wings.

31
00:00:57,370 --> 00:00:57,930
One!

32
00:00:58,090 --> 00:00:59,380
Look at its feathers.

33
00:00:59,883 --> 00:01:01,683
Birds live largely on land.

34
00:01:01,903 --> 00:01:04,733
Birds have beaks that enable them to pick up food.

35
00:01:04,947 --> 00:01:07,317
Birds have wings and can usually fly.

36
00:01:07,521 --> 00:01:11,051
Some birds such as ostriches and penguins cannot fly.

37
00:01:11,258 --> 00:01:12,478
Birds lay eggs.

38
00:01:13,063 --> 00:01:14,173
Say it with me!

39
00:01:14,882 --> 00:01:17,062
Birds have an outer covering of feathers.

40
00:01:21,509 --> 00:01:22,769
The answer is one.

41
00:01:22,999 --> 00:01:24,479
A penguin has feathers.

42
00:01:24,699 --> 00:01:25,939
So it is a bird.

43
00:01:25,989 --> 00:01:27,789
So flying is not the clue.

44
00:01:28,009 --> 00:01:29,149
Feathers are!

45
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:31,330
One finger?

46
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:32,740
One finger up!

47
00:01:33,317 --> 00:01:35,157
Now look down, into the water.

48
00:01:35,417 --> 00:01:36,267
A fish!

49
00:01:36,389 --> 00:01:39,609
Fish are animals that usually live only in water.

50
00:01:39,809 --> 00:01:42,089
They have fins to help them swim in water.

51
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:45,720
Say it with me!

52
00:01:46,427 --> 00:01:48,707
Fish have an outer covering of scales.

53
00:01:53,232 --> 00:01:55,272
Fish usually breathe through their gills.

54
00:01:57,459 --> 00:01:59,759
Some fish, such as cod, lay eggs.

55
00:01:59,979 --> 00:02:03,559
Other fish, such as the guppy and some sharks, give birth to

56
00:02:03,309 --> 00:02:04,439
their young alive.

57
00:02:05,727 --> 00:02:06,647
Round two.

58
00:02:06,907 --> 00:02:07,877
Look at the mud!

59
00:02:08,137 --> 00:02:10,157
This animal hops about on land.

60
00:02:10,367 --> 00:02:12,647
But it has fins, scales and gills.

61
00:02:12,867 --> 00:02:13,747
What is it?

62
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,317
One, an amphibian.

63
00:02:15,547 --> 00:02:16,577
Two, a bird.

64
00:02:16,837 --> 00:02:17,857
Three, a fish.

65
00:02:18,087 --> 00:02:19,497
Show me with your fingers.

66
00:02:24,969 --> 00:02:25,919
Locked in!

67
00:02:26,049 --> 00:02:26,639
One!

68
00:02:26,769 --> 00:02:27,749
Land and water.

69
00:02:27,969 --> 00:02:29,259
Just like the frog!

70
00:02:29,309 --> 00:02:30,109
Three.

71
00:02:30,309 --> 00:02:32,629
I count fins, scales and gills.

72
00:02:32,684 --> 00:02:33,504
Three!

73
00:02:33,604 --> 00:02:34,894
Frogs have legs.

74
00:02:34,954 --> 00:02:36,164
It has fins.

75
00:02:36,668 --> 00:02:37,808
Be the mudskipper!

76
00:02:38,058 --> 00:02:39,028
Shrink down.

77
00:02:39,248 --> 00:02:40,128
Quietly.

78
00:02:42,515 --> 00:02:43,815
You are a mudskipper.

79
00:02:44,175 --> 00:02:45,315
You are in the water.

80
00:02:45,775 --> 00:02:47,345
You breathe through your gills.

81
00:02:47,944 --> 00:02:49,374
The tide goes out.

82
00:02:49,684 --> 00:02:51,114
The water gets shallow.

83
00:02:52,428 --> 00:02:53,898
You push with your fins.

84
00:02:54,238 --> 00:02:54,948
Hop.

85
00:02:55,298 --> 00:02:55,998
Hop.

86
00:02:56,328 --> 00:02:57,548
You are on the mud.

87
00:02:58,132 --> 00:03:00,642
Now, on land, you breathe through your skin.

88
00:03:01,309 --> 00:03:03,099
Fins, scales and gills.

89
00:03:03,419 --> 00:03:04,789
You are still a fish.

90
00:03:07,211 --> 00:03:08,551
The answer is three.

91
00:03:08,675 --> 00:03:12,705
Mudskippers are special fish that can live on land as well as

92
00:03:12,455 --> 00:03:13,245
in water.

93
00:03:14,461 --> 00:03:15,521
Three fingers?

94
00:03:15,741 --> 00:03:16,901
One finger up!

95
00:03:18,477 --> 00:03:19,837
My field notes!

96
00:03:19,961 --> 00:03:20,611
One.

97
00:03:20,751 --> 00:03:22,371
A frog is an amphibian.

98
00:03:22,471 --> 00:03:23,261
Two.

99
00:03:23,311 --> 00:03:24,711
A penguin is a bird.

100
00:03:24,851 --> 00:03:25,741
Three.

101
00:03:25,781 --> 00:03:27,421
A starfish is a fish.

102
00:03:27,772 --> 00:03:28,652
Showdown!

103
00:03:28,892 --> 00:03:29,982
Double points.

104
00:03:30,222 --> 00:03:31,802
One line has a mistake.

105
00:03:32,032 --> 00:03:33,742
Line one, two, or three?

106
00:03:33,972 --> 00:03:35,382
Show me with your fingers.

107
00:03:41,850 --> 00:03:42,800
Locked in!

108
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:43,740
Three.

109
00:03:43,950 --> 00:03:45,870
A starfish has no scales.

110
00:03:45,923 --> 00:03:46,613
Three!

111
00:03:46,733 --> 00:03:47,853
And no gills.

112
00:03:47,899 --> 00:03:48,469
Oops!

113
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:50,160
Fixed!

114
00:03:49,910 --> 00:03:51,530
Not a fish.

115
00:03:51,655 --> 00:03:53,125
Starfish are not fish!

116
00:03:53,345 --> 00:03:56,045
This is because they do not have scales or gills.

117
00:03:56,183 --> 00:03:57,513
Showed three fingers?

118
00:03:57,703 --> 00:03:59,603
Put up two more on your score hand!

119
00:04:00,104 --> 00:04:01,144
Three stamps!

120
00:04:01,424 --> 00:04:02,874
Three animal groups.

121
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:04,676
Say it with us!

122
00:04:05,337 --> 00:04:05,987
Frog!

123
00:04:05,749 --> 00:04:06,400
Bird!

124
00:04:06,162 --> 00:04:06,872
Fish!

125
00:04:08,637 --> 00:04:10,387
Moist skin, feathers, scales!

126
00:04:11,937 --> 00:04:12,587
Frog!

127
00:04:12,349 --> 00:04:12,999
Bird!

128
00:04:12,762 --> 00:04:13,472
Fish!

129
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:15,337
Moist skin, feathers, scales!

130
00:04:16,192 --> 00:04:17,572
Show me your score hand!

131
00:04:17,812 --> 00:04:18,822
More than two?

132
00:04:19,062 --> 00:04:20,332
You beat the Buddies.

133
00:04:20,562 --> 00:04:21,612
Four fingers?

134
00:04:21,852 --> 00:04:22,832
High five!

135
00:04:23,336 --> 00:04:24,706
Did you spot the frog?

136
00:04:24,966 --> 00:04:26,496
It was on a mangrove root!

137
00:04:26,716 --> 00:04:27,986
Tell someone at home.

138
00:04:29,386 --> 00:04:33,566
Three more animal groups to go: insects, reptiles and mammals.

139
00:04:33,776 --> 00:04:34,896
Here is an ant.

140
00:04:35,116 --> 00:04:36,146
And a spider.

141
00:04:36,376 --> 00:04:37,886
Only one is an insect!

142
00:04:38,096 --> 00:04:40,346
Can you tell which, by counting its legs?

143
00:04:40,566 --> 00:04:42,466
Lock in your answer for next time.

144
00:04:43,187 --> 00:04:45,347
Let's read today's key words together!

145
00:04:45,587 --> 00:04:46,307
Ready?

146
00:04:46,597 --> 00:04:47,367
Feathers.

147
00:04:48,728 --> 00:04:49,376
Fins.

148
00:04:50,722 --> 00:04:51,448
Scales.

149
00:04:52,924 --> 00:04:53,576
Gills.

150
00:04:54,899 --> 00:04:55,799
Well done!

151
00:04:56,782 --> 00:04:57,841
Say it with us!

152
00:04:58,641 --> 00:04:59,351
Ready?

153
00:04:59,475 --> 00:05:00,095
One!

154
00:05:00,475 --> 00:05:01,155
two!

155
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:02,655
Now you know!
